Workstream ID: streak-fire-history
Title: Add realistic streak fire and an original recorded-work calendar
Status: DONE
Milestone: Deliver a coherent, truthful streak experience across mission and navigation
Dependencies: compact-square-chrome, mission-clarity
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/36
Purpose: A nonzero mission streak should look alight with realistic turbulent
  flames, not a cartoon icon. Zero should feel like an extinguished campfire.
  Any running mission streak also lights the compact navbar calendar.
  Provide one original, polished page for all running streaks, date ranges,
  recorded-day intensity and historical runs, without inventing activity.

Tasks:
  [x] Read the actual mission activity, header, navigation and motion policies.
  [x] Extend the existing local-calendar projection with days and real runs.
  [x] Implement original bounded realistic fire and cold campfire presentation.
  [x] Preserve frosted square framing, readable counts and motion safeguards.
  [x] Connect any-mission activity to the existing compact navbar calendar.
  [x] Add Streaks navigation, an original activity calendar and run history.
  [x] Cover both themes, narrow layouts, date boundaries and real data guards.
  [x] Update focused documentation, original tracking and owned continuity.
  [x] Publish the coherent steered scope and verify exact CI and hosted output.

Acceptance criteria:
  Positive mission streaks use actual animated turbulent flame imagery with
    bright cores, rolling orange tongues and embers, rather than a flame icon.
    Zero uses charred logs/cool ash and no active flame animation.
  New artwork remains inside sharp frosted-glass framing. Counts and actual
    recorded-day states stay readable; do not make zero an error or failure.
  The navbar lights whenever any mission's genuine streak is nonzero,
    irrespective of primary/in-focus mode or a selected history filter.
    Preserve the restored69/60pxheader,40x50pxcalendar and red weekend strip.
  One Streaks page shows current mission runs, actual start/end dates and an
    original non-copy activity calendar, including selected-day record detail.
    Derive intensity from saved evidence/recall, not attention or timer use.
  Existing local-day deduplication, yesterday-ending continuity, future-day
    exclusion and archived-version records remain authoritative.
  Fire has a visible pause mechanism, authoritative reduced motion, hidden/
    offscreen/dialog suspension and cleanup. Bound CPU, resolution and frame
    rate; do not add another WebGL context, dependency or external media fetch.
  History/filter/year/day navigation is read-only and keyboard/touch usable.
    No schema/default/reward/journal or owner browser-data change.
  Preserve the already pushed b9bba6c correction and its exact known watcher.
    Technical checks, human visual acceptance and publication remain separate.
  Keep the original numbered workstream/issue/Project identity and public-safe
    evidence. Do not copy private progress, context, PDFs or credentials.

